> @cvinayak The ISO broadcast does not yet have data path, right? So we can't send SDUs from the host, but isn't it still sending some dummy data?

@Thalley The issue is reported in use of Packetcraft Controller. `<inf> bt_hci_core: HCI: version 5.2 (0x0b) revision 0x0ce5, manufacturer 0x07e8`

Preliminary data path is supported in Zephyr Controller. iso_broadcast and iso_receive samples should be working with datapath using Zephyr Controller, this is based on the fact that bsim_test_iso continues to pass in PR CI.
